Z||000000||count_iblis||12-21-2000||12:01 AM||||The more I see the over head scoop the more I want it!  What all do you have to do to make it functional?<BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/count-sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Oreif||12-21-2000||02:03 AM||||To make my scoop functional I had to cut out the face and come up with a different mount. The latch/hinge mount that comes with it blocks 2/3's of the airflow. I cut a 9" X 3" hole and mounted an aluminum plate to it. I also put a stainless steel screen over the face to keep debris out of it. The only drawback is you need to remove the scoop to open the decklid.<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Scoop_2.jpg">  <P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 12-21-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||LZeitgeist||12-21-2000||02:26 AM||||Where does one acquire one of these scoops?||||reg||1
Z||000003||Philphine||12-21-2000||02:59 AM||||mine is kind of functional. there is a 5" round hole under mine with the air intake from my air cleaner hacked up and routed under it. sounds kind of neat with the sunroof open. looks bad though since i didn't want to go through a lot of trouble working up something for the 4cyl. when i want to change it. i reworked the mounting too but it's still fairly close to the instructions as far as the hinge and latch.<P>irm and focoa sell them. want one for my indy also.||||reg||1
Z||000004||count_iblis||12-21-2000||03:02 AM||||can someone post a link or a pic of the wrap around air scoops.  they are like the overhead but they wrap around to the side.  Where can I find these at?  <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/count-sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||firstfiero||12-21-2000||09:04 AM||||   I want one...I don't need it to be functional....I WANT ONE! Their are bad as HELL!   86se||||reg||6
Z||000006||Oreif||12-21-2000||09:53 AM||||The scoops are available thru:<BR>IRM  1-800-367-8423 or IRMFIERO@aol.com<BR>(They call it an Indy Scoop)<P>and also<BR> <A HREF="http://www.showcars-bodyparts.com/fiero.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.showcars-bodyparts.com/fiero.html</A> <BR>(They call it an SD4 street scoop)<P>As for the twin Fi-Air-O scoops, I don't know who's making them. But from what I hear they are no good without a fan because the scoops hook onto the grates and the engine compartment was designed to push the hot air out the grates and the scoops try to force it down. (I personally don't like the look of them.)<P><BR>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 12-21-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||2xsess||12-21-2000||10:02 AM||||Are these the ones you're talking about Count?<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/lazycscoops.jpg"> <P>Here's the link <A HREF="http://www.fieroowners.com/store1.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroowners.com/store1.htm</A> <BR><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/My_car_(large)sig_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000008||1FST2M6||12-21-2000||10:56 AM||||bad thing about the wrap around ones is they won't work on the GTs! they are nice looking... (disrupt the air flow more than being functional... but sure look sweet) I'm sure you could easily manipulate them to work on a GT.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Oreif||12-21-2000||11:30 AM||||WOW are FOCOA prices high. $355 for an indy scoop opened up and $330 normally. The "Lazy C's" are $330 per pair. IRM charges $200 for the indy scoop. Not sure about the SD4 version. I heard it was $230 but that is unconfirmed.||||reg||1
