Z||000017||count_iblis||12-22-2000||08:43 PM||||cooter do you have more pics or info on yours?  that is what im thinking about doing<BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/count-sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000018||Cooter||12-22-2000||09:24 PM||||I will look and see if I can find the other pic's of the setup I made. Basically, the air filter is a clamp on K-N for a speed density Tuned Port Injection that fits directly on the throttle body. I used the "snorkle" (the part of the air filter housing that the plastic duct snaps onto)from a full size GM truck air filter to clamp the K-N on to. Then I used some sheet metal to make a small air box to attach the snorkle to. A piece of 2 inch pipe comes out of the side of the air box and is attached to the throttle body with a piece of flexible hose. It sounds more complicated than it really is, I promise!||||reg||1
Z||000019||Oreif||12-23-2000||02:48 AM||||Mine isn't "Ram Air" into the intake at present, I am using it for cooling. Engine compartment temps are over 20 degrees cooler. I have thought about ducting it into the engine but I want to do it so the intake hose isn't connected to the decklid. Simular to the old GTO's. Airfilter box is attached to engine and the decklid acts as the airfilter cover with a foam seal. ||||reg||1
