Z||000023||Philphine||12-24-2000||06:37 PM||||got one on my '87. functional as an air intake but not nessesarily ram air since any pressure that could be developed would just rush around the the air cleaner intake. i didn't seal it off so i guess the engine gets a little cool air like oreif's. <P>i'd like to see how the scoop on the real indy's routed air. was it functional? anybody got any pics of the real indy engine bay?||||reg||1
Z||000024||Oreif||12-24-2000||10:21 PM||||The REAL Pace cars used SD4 engines. So the Aircleaner was like the old Pontiac Ram Air type. Open top with sides that met the decklid that had a foam seal. Look at a 4cyl Fiero and you'll see it is much easier to duct since the throttle body is right on top near the center. The V-6 points to the drivers side so it is harder to duct it without restricting it or using lots of tight curves.||||reg||1
